Sigh, another promising wizard gone.

I'm a neutral male gnomish wizard.  I make a successful protection run
and get some cool armor (+3 studded leather, +4 elvish cap).
I find AoR in Sokoban.  Have a big stash of unID'd scrolls/potions in
minetown.  Find a spellbook of Cone of Cold, and some others.  No magic
missile or ID yet.

Train a new pet cat and drag it onto a polytrap in the mines until it
morphs into a white Dragon.

My pet D eats the crossaligned priest so I have no problem converting
the altar (2x bag of trix) and soon get magicbane.  Somwhere along the
way I stumble upon GoP.

I venture further down the mines.  There is another polytrap there, and
a Master Mind Flayer which I manage to dispens of with judicious use of
the E-word (fast-engraved using 'bane), my pet D and some flying
daggers.

I find the 3rd! polytrap in the mines.  A horde of orcs appears on the
other side of it and each one of them is ithcin-for-a-changin' cause
they all jump on the trap.  This yields among other minor pests two D's
(orange and grey).
Ring of conflict + E-word + flying daggers takes care of that (still
unenchanted btw).

The carnage leaves 2 dragon corpses and 2 scales.  I think I remember
something about dragons confering intrinsics, so I try for the orange
corpse but my pet D is to quick for me.  I eat the gray one instead and
get a message that I can barely finish it, but no "do you want to
continue" message.

Alright, time to drag the scales to my stash, buc-id them and hope I
can write some scrolls of enchanct armor (I have 1 uncursed and 1
cursed magic marker).  Btw, how many charges does it take to write a
scroll?  How 'bout a spellbook?

A gelatinous cube appears along the way and starts freezing me.  I beat
it into submission with some D help, and again I think I remember
something about gel.cubes confering intrinsics.  "Waste not want not" I
say and eat away.

I choke.  No warning.  No "this is hard to finish. do you want to
contine".  Nothing.  Bah!

Why is it that you sometimes are warned you are about to choke, and
sometimes not?  Doesn't that seem unfair to anyone, and designed to
trap people into these kinds of mistakes?  Either have the warning or
